WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.580
Hello.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:11.190
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.130
This is the third session.

4
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:20.010
Even with the same mood disorder, the way mood
moves over time differs from person to person.

5
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.070
Today, we will look at the main
courses one by one, in graphs.

6
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.620
The horizontal line in the middle is your usual mood.

7
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.760
Going up means hypomania and mania.

8
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.340
Going down means depressive episodes
and major depressive episodes.

9
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.960
Red shows elevated periods.

10
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.860
Blue shows depressed periods.

11
00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.430
First is typical depression.

12
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.810
Only depression appears, with no mania or hypomania,

13
00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:54.980
and it is common when it starts in middle age or later.

14
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.760
Between episodes, mood is fairly
stable without big mood swings,

15
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.470
and it tends to respond well to antidepressants.

16
00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:09.530
But without treatment, more than half of
people become depressed again within one year.

17
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:15.540
Relapse is that common, and untreated
depression may also raise the risk of dementia.

18
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:21.825
Next is bipolar I disorder with
clearly separate episodes.

19
00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:28.380
There are definite manic periods, and
hospital admission is often needed then.

20
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.500
Mania usually appears once every one
to two years, or every few years.

21
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.740
In severe cases, it can appear several times a year.

22
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.880
Between episodes, mood stays fairly steady.

23
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.900
But relapses are frequent, and each
relapse makes the next one more likely.

24
00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:53.460
If hallucinations or delusions occur, it can
sometimes be hard to tell from schizophrenia.

25
00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.779
Even within bipolar I, some people
still have symptoms between episodes,

26
00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:02.390
and their mood swings continue.

27
00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:06.261
Because of the mania, the diagnosis is bipolar I.

28
00:02:06.281 --> 00:02:11.805
But they also have the difficulties of
bipolar II, with marked mood swings,

29
00:02:11.825 --> 00:02:15.210
so they need even steadier treatment and care.

30
00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:23.630
Bipolar II disorder has no mania, but it
has hypomania and major depressive episodes.

31
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:29.130
Most of the time is spent depressed,
and the hypomania passes quickly.

32
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:35.330
So it is easy to be diagnosed with simple
depression or a personality problem.

33
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.710
After hypomania comes depression
at least three times as long.

34
00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:45.270
The depressed period can last up to
thirty times longer than the hypomania.

35
00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:51.170
If the illness is not diagnosed
and only antidepressants are taken,

36
00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:59.000
mood cycles may speed up or hypomania may appear,
and treatment can gradually become harder.

37
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:06.000
Other conditions often come with it, such as
self-harm, suicide attempts, panic disorder,

38
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.840
or alcohol problems.

39
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:11.100
So especially careful treatment is needed.

40
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:19.310
In cyclothymic disorder, mild lows
and mild highs come and go often,

41
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.180
and mood is always unstable.

42
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.600
So people may be mistaken for having a
moody personality or big emotional swings.

43
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.480
It is easy to miss unless the doctor
specializes in mood disorders.

44
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:40.400
If depression began in the teens or twenties,
or keeps recurring or swings widely,

45
00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:46.140
we must always consider that cyclothymic
disorder may have been there before.

46
00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:52.067
There is also depression with mood
swings but without mania or hypomania.

47
00:03:52.087 --> 00:03:58.700
It resembles bipolar II, but with less
energy, so hypomania is not clearly visible.

48
00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.560
It may not improve with simple depression treatment,

49
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:06.620
or it may be diagnosed as
borderline personality disorder.

50
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:11.390
The risk of self-harm or suicidal
thoughts is often even higher.

51
00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:16.710
When these people are elevated, they feel
irritable and impulsive rather than good,

52
00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.970
which is sometimes called dark hypomania.

53
00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:23.890
Treatment along the lines of bipolar disorder is needed.

54
00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:28.960
Agitated depression is depression where restlessness and

55
00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.700
anxiety stand out more than
low mood or loss of motivation.

56
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.060
Often, a person who was lively
and diligent faces a major stress,

57
00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:45.240
then repeatedly tries to force their mood up
without success, and the mood swings grow.

58
00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:49.340
Thoughts do not stop, so it is hard to fall asleep.

59
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.240
They may cry often, and sometimes think about suicide.

60
00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:59.560
It can also show up as chest tightness,
like hwabyung, or as various pains.

61
00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.880
Impatience to get better quickly
can actually make symptoms worse,

62
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.360
and sometimes a mood stabilizer
or an antipsychotic is needed.

63
00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:13.270
Double depression is when severe depression appears on

64
00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:17.690
top of mild depression that has lasted a long time.

65
00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.870
People feel they have always been depressed.

66
00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:28.060
The symptoms are so long-standing that it is
easy to think it is personality, not illness.

67
00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.180
Simple antidepressants may not be enough,

68
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:36.480
and the mood stabilizer lithium
is known to be effective.

69
00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:37.901
There are other courses too: depression
that suddenly turns into mania,

70
00:05:37.921 --> 00:05:49.320
or cases where changes in thinking, motivation,
or sensation stand out more than mood,

71
00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.989
or cases made harder by panic attacks,
pain, or trouble concentrating.

72
00:05:57.009 --> 00:05:58.770
Mood disorders show a great variety of courses.

73
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:03.340
Recording your mood steadily in a mood journal helps

74
00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.980
you notice early signs of relapse and respond to them.

75
00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.920
Next time, we will talk about why mood
disorders happen: causes and temperament.

76
00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.160
Thank you.
